# 13. RESPONSIVE BACKGROUND BEHAVIOR

A global background needs responsive composition rules.

### Desktop

Maintain broad glass shapes and atmospheric lighting.

Preserve large negative spaces.

### Tablet

Reposition optical elements so they do not interfere with narrower content layouts.

Maintain a consistent line pattern.

### Mobile

Reduce decorative complexity.

Use fewer visible large glass shapes.

Keep the primary email form readable.

Avoid overly dense line patterns.

Keep the global surface continuous even as sections become much taller.

### Critical mobile issue

Do not calculate background geometry only once at initial page load.

Fonts, images, responsive stacking, and content expansion can change the total document height.

Use robust layout measurements where necessary.

Avoid expensive continuous resize observers if CSS positioning can solve the problem.

Preserve visual continuity during orientation changes.

